.TH CAST 1 "October 2026" "cast 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cast \- presentation camera, recorder and RTMP streamer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cast
[options] [command]
.SH DESCRIPTION
cast opens the app and starts or attaches to one daemon. cast \-\-headless runs
the daemon in the terminal for scripts and services. cast COMMAND sends a bounded request to its
user\-only Unix socket and prints acknowledged success or an actionable error. Exit 0
means success; errors exit nonzero. \-\-help, \-\-version and COMMAND \-\-help run locally.
config check/defaults and doctor also run locally without a daemon. Runtime arguments
are never passed to a shell. Concurrent commands are ordered by accepted connection;
messages are atomic and a silent peer has a bounded timeout. A client timeout means
completion is unknown: inspect status before repeating a non\-idempotent command.
.PP
Startup flags appear before the command: \-\-headless, \-\-config PATH, \-\-socket PATH,
\-\-backend xorg|wayland, \-\-output\-device PATH, \-\-camera\-device PATH,
\-\-width N, \-\-height N, \-\-fps N, \-\-no\-virtual, \-\-no\-camera,
\-\-mic\-source NAME, \-\-desktop\-source NAME, \-\-record\-dir PATH,
\-\-container NAME, \-\-video\-codec NAME, \-\-audio\-codec NAME, \-\-countdown SECONDS.
Selecting an audio source does not enable its lane: configure or explicitly enable it.
Build features decide backend availability. synthetic backend/camera and none output
are explicitly test\-only options; they do not represent working desktop/device access.
.PP
layout overlay|stage|split|screen|camera selects composition; layout next|prev follows
composition.layout_order. split side left|right chooses camera side; split ratio 25%
sets its share. Camera hidden state and geometry persist when changing layouts.
.PP
camera show|hide|toggle sets visibility; toggle reverses only visibility.
camera size +5%|\-5%|25% adjusts five percentage points or sets 25% of canvas width.
Anchored resizing fixes that corner, free sizing fixes center, and valid positions
are clamped within the canvas. Impossible sizes fail. camera move DX DY is relative;
camera position X Y is absolute output pixels, and both switch to free positioning.
camera anchor top\-left|top\-right|bottom\-left|bottom\-right|top|bottom|left|right|next|prev
selects a corner or the middle of an edge. Edge resizing retains the margin and
centering; next follows camera.corner_order, which may include edge anchors.
camera shape rectangle|rounded|circle|next|prev cycles rectangle→rounded→circle.
camera aspect native|16:9|4:3|1:1|next|prev controls centered crop independently of mask;
circle forces square crop. camera crop move DX DY adjusts source\-pixel crop offsets.
camera mirror on|off|toggle affects camera content only and defaults to on; the screen
stays unmirrored. Use cast camera mirror off to disable it for the session, or set
mirror = false in [camera] for a persistent default. camera list enumerates
camera formats/devices. camera device PATH acquires the candidate before replacing
current camera; permissions/format errors are actionable.
.PP
screen list, screen select NAME and screen next|prev discover/select/cycle Xorg
RandR monitors. capture monitor selects the current monitor; on Wayland it opens
portal consent again. capture region X Y WIDTH HEIGHT uses selected\-monitor pixels.
capture region select starts an interactive drag; capture window select starts a
click selection; capture window active selects the currently active window once.
Interactive commands acknowledge acquisition start, keep the prior source until
commit, and Escape cancels. status shows resulting source/errors. Window resize,
movement and failures are handled without silently returning to the desktop.
capture fit contain|cover selects letterboxing or cropping. Source changes reset
zoom and annotation history, and do not resume any output. Unsupported backend
selection commands fail explicitly.
.PP
On Xorg, panel and native-preview overlap in monitor/region captures is filled with
capture.mask_color. capture mask\-color '#112233' or settings capture.mask_color
'#112233' changes it at runtime; [capture] mask_color sets a persistent default.
The color is independent of the pause background and applies to virtual camera,
recording and streaming. Changing it preserves output states and zoom. Countdown
guides use the same opaque mask. Live underlying desktop reconstruction and
transparent exclusion are unavailable; remove any unreleased capture.exclusion
configuration field. Wayland does not support this masking.
.PP
zoom toggle alternates 1 and the last/configured non\-1 factor; zoom in|out
adds/subtracts zoom.step within limits; zoom set FACTOR sets a finite factor;
zoom reset returns to 1. zoom follow on|off selects smoothed cursor tracking or
locks the target. Screen zoom leaves camera and annotation labels unscaled.
cursor on|off|toggle controls the separately rendered pointer;
cursor highlight on|off|toggle changes its highlight. Embedded cursor policy
needs portal restart; there is no second pointer. Cursor metadata is required for
follow/highlighting. clicks on|off|toggle controls mouse rings. keys on|off|toggle
controls recent key labels; keys mode shortcuts|all selects shortcuts/navigation or
explicit printable events; keys clear discards labels. All keys can expose private
text. Raw observations are never written to an input log. Compose/IME events do
not universally reproduce committed text; keyboard names/layout translation are
best effort. Consecutive identical labels collapse as j, jx2, jx3. A bounded
queue retains recent labels for keys.timeout_ms (3000 ms by default); repeat
counts refresh that row, and older rows expire independently.
Configure keys.filter to exclude every cast\-control shortcut you bind.
annotations virtual|record|stream keys|clicks on|off selects annotation visibility per lane.
.PP
pause solid-pauses both applicable outputs and cancels pending start/cut-resume
countdown. Recording continues writing neutral video and silence. resume restores
only remembered solid states, never starts a recording or clears a cut. Independent
solid commands supersede remembered restoration; freeze/blur/cut preserve it.
.PP
virtual pause|resume|toggle controls solid privacy pause. virtual freeze|unfreeze
holds/releases screen and camera together. virtual blur [on|off|toggle] applies a
configurable blurred/tinted composition with optional title/subtitle/footer; bare blur
turns it on, unblur turns it off. Blur overlays freeze; solid pause overrides both.
Pause/freeze/blur silence cast audio. Blur can leave content recognizable: use solid
pause for privacy. Neither unfreeze nor unblur resumes a solid pause.
.PP
virtual message "TEXT" changes the shared solid-pause title without changing output
states. Empty title/subtitle/footer values are valid. settings output.pause_title TEXT,
output.pause_subtitle TEXT, output.pause_background #RRGGBB and
output.pause_foreground #RRGGBB edit solid-screen style. The corresponding blur_title,
blur_subtitle, blur_color, blur_foreground, blur_radius (1..128) and blur_opacity
(0..1) control blur. pause_text/pause_color remain aliases. Fonts pause_font and
blur_font are config-file-only, default Noto Sans, applied through config reload.
The optional pause_footer/blur_footer is centered near the bottom. Footer sizes
pause_footer_size/blur_footer_size default to 18 output pixels (8..256).
pause_text_gap/blur_text_gap set title/subtitle distance independently of font size
(0..512 output pixels, default 12). virtual/record footer TEXT changes the shared
solid-pause footer; settings output.blur_footer TEXT changes the blur footer.
Titles allow 127 UTF-8 bytes; subtitles and footers allow 255. {date}, {time}, {datetime} expand
in local time; a colon adds a strftime format, e.g. {date:%Y-%m-%d} or {time:%H:%M}.
Double braces {{ and }} produce literal braces. Invalid templates fail atomically.
.PP
record start [PATH] creates one file without overwriting. record stop requests
finalization; status --json reports record.finalizing; quit waits for completion.
record pause writes the solid title/subtitle/footer screen and silence. record resume clears
solid pause unless cut; record toggle toggles solid pause, never cut/start/stop.
record freeze|unfreeze and record blur [on|off|toggle] / unblur match virtual effects,
with independent flags and shared styles.
.PP
record cut interrupts video/audio file admission. record resume from cut reuses the
record.countdown start delay, then continues the SAME file with interruption and
countdown time removed. Existing solid/freeze/blur flags remain. record cut again
cancels a pending resume and retains the file. These controls need a recording.
Migration from v0.3: use record cut where record pause previously removed time.
.PP
On Xorg, the film-style guide opens in CastPreview even when preview was off,
whether or not the panel is attached. It closes completely
and preview toggles off before recording starts/resumes; this includes a previously
enabled preview. Escape/closing cancels the action. WM decorations must disappear
before admission; a hide failure cancels start/resume. Guides never enter the file.
Wayland panel displays countdown status; native countdown preview is unsupported.
.PP
audio list lists PipeWire sources. audio mic|desktop|virtual on|off|toggle controls
lanes/virtual source; audio mic|desktop source NAME selects explicitly;
audio mic|desktop gain 80% sets gain (0..400%). Desktop capture requires an explicit
source; it starts off. A speaker\-monitor source can include call participants;
application capture avoids broad mixes where PipeWire supports it. Disappearing
sources silence the lane and report errors; there is no broad\-source fallback.
Virtual camera pause/freeze/blur silences cast's optional virtual microphone. A physical mic selected
directly by a conference app needs the app's own mute control. cast creates no
physical\-speaker playback route; video and audio devices are selected separately.
.PP
preset NAME|next|prev applies composition\-only named settings and configured cycle.
preview on|off|toggle controls local preview; preview target virtual|record|stream chooses
its lane. Local RUNNING/PAUSED/FROZEN/RECORDING labels stay out of exported frames.
status [\-\-json] reports capabilities, source, layout, camera visibility, zoom,
virtual/record state, path/active duration/countdown/finalization, audio routing, errors and drops.
doctor performs read\-only dependency/device/directory checks with setup advice.
setup prints virtual\-camera and conferencing instructions without changing the system.
completions [bash|zsh|fish] prints shell setup instructions;
completions \-\-script SHELL emits its embedded completion script.
update [vMAJOR.MINOR[.PATCH]] [\-\-download\-only DIRECTORY] downloads an official
Arch x86_64 release package and verifies its SHA\-256 checksum. With no version,
it selects the latest release. Installation uses pacman and sudo when needed;
download\-only saves the checked package without installing. Stop cast before an
update and restart afterwards. These commands do not require a running daemon.
panel opens the optional native control panel (build with PANEL=1) without
automatically starting a daemon. Start launches one when stopped. Bare cast starts
a daemon after its app window is ready. Close leaves outputs running. Stop daemon
saves recording and keeps the panel open; Start retains acknowledged session settings
and original startup flags, with virtual output paused and record/stream stopped.
Quit confirms before clean shutdown. cast\-app and the installed Cast application
entry open the same app; headless builds omit these launchers.
settings SECTION.KEY VALUE [SECTION.KEY VALUE ...]
applies an atomic session batch using the INI schema and reload restrictions.
Invalid batches leave current settings intact.
.PP
config check [PATH], config defaults, config reload validate/print/reload config.
reset restores effective composition defaults only; quit cleanly shuts down
and finalizes an existing recording. No command persists session changes to config.
.PP
For a status bar, poll cast status \-\-json and parse JSON, for example
cast status \-\-json | jq \-r '.virtual.state + " / " + .record.state'.
The last_error field retains the last reported failure; errors are also printed
by the terminal daemon or appended to SOCKET.log beside an app\-launched daemon socket. A successful unrelated command does not erase evidence.
.PP
When an edited configuration is invalid, explicit \-\-socket PATH runtime commands
use that routing directly, so status and config reload remain reachable. Local
config check/doctor and daemon startup still strictly validate the selected file.
.SH FILES
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cast/cast.conf or $HOME/.config/cast/cast.conf
.PP
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cast.sock
.SH SCREEN STYLE AND BRANDING
Stage places an inset screen opposite the camera anchor; both preserve aspect
ratio and overlap only as their chosen sizes require. screen size PERCENT changes
stage width, screen margin PIXELS sets its inset, screen radius PIXELS sets rounded corners, and screen border
width PIXELS or screen border color #RRGGBB sets its border. Styling applies to
all screen layers. screen background blurred|gradient|solid chooses the backdrop.
.PP
settings background.source screen|camera chooses the blurred screen/stage source.
The shared background.gradient_from/via/to colors, gradient_via_enabled boolean,
gradient_angle (0..360 degrees) and gradient_waypoint (1..99 percent) configure
screen and camera gradient modes. The via stop is optional.
.PP
logo on|off|toggle, path PATH, size PERCENT, anchor ANCHOR, margin X Y and opacity
0..1 place a transparent local image. text on|off|toggle, set TEXT, font FONT,
size PIXELS, color #RRGGBB, anchor ANCHOR, margin X Y and opacity 0..1 place
static UTF-8 text. Corners and edge centers are supported. Margins use output
pixels. Static text does not expand placeholders. Solid pause replaces branding;
freeze and blur include it. Composition commands never resume outputs.
.PP
Every next cycle also accepts prev, wrapping backwards through the same configured
order. These commands change session settings; cast never writes user config.
.SH SEE ALSO
sxhkd(1), ffmpeg(1), pw-cli(1)

.SH STREAMING
cast stream start opens one RTMP/RTMPS destination asynchronously, privacy-paused.
cast stream resume explicitly reveals the composition; connection success alone
never reveals it. stop ends transmission and cancels every retry.
.PP
stream pause|resume|toggle, freeze|unfreeze, blur [on|off|toggle], and unblur require
an existing session. Resume clears solid pause only; blur remains above freeze.
Solid pause, freeze and blur send silence. Streaming keeps continuous media time
and has no recording-style cut operation. stream status [\-\-json] reports local
lifecycle, presentation, write/queue/drop/retry statistics and sanitized errors;
network writes do not prove service or viewer delivery.
.PP
settings stream.KEY VALUE changes the session only. Connection/encoder settings
are locked while active: stop first. Store only an absolute stream-key file path
in [stream]. It must be a regular file owned by you, with mode 600, no symlinks,
and one nonempty line. Edit it locally; never put the actual secret in a command,
URL, config, or panel field. RTMPS verifies certificates and hostnames.
.PP
preview target virtual|record|stream selects a lane. annotations stream keys|clicks
on|off controls streaming annotations. virtual start|stop enables/disables local
virtual-camera output independently; start is privacy-paused.
.SH MIGRATION
The old live command is now virtual; \-\-no\-live is \-\-no\-virtual.
preview target live becomes virtual. annotations.live_keys/live_clicks become
annotations.virtual_keys/virtual_clicks. Status JSON uses virtual and stream objects.
Old spellings fail with migration instructions and execute no operation.
